{"id": "EUVD-2026-80462", "enisaUuid": "26a9d9d5-d247-38a5-b4ee-371cd864485e", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nscsi: qla2xxx: Fix BSG job leak on validate flash image error path\n\nqla28xx_validate_flash_image() returns QLA_SUCCESS (0) unconditionally,\ntelling the FC BSG transport (fc_bsg_host_dispatch()) that the driver\nowns and will complete the request. But bsg_job_done() is guarded by \"if\n(!rval)\", so on the error path (rval == -EINVAL) neither the driver nor\nthe transport completes the job. The request dangles until it times out,\nleaking block layer resources.\n\nCommit c2c68225b145 (\"scsi: qla2xxx: Fix bsg_done() causing double\nfree\") added the \"if (!rval)\" guard to a batch of BSG handlers. That is\ncorrect for handlers that also return the error code (the transport then\ncompletes the job once via fail_host_msg), but this function returns\nQLA_SUCCESS unconditionally, so the guard turned a correct single\ncompletion into a leak.\n\nAlways call bsg_job_done(): bsg_reply->result is DID_OK and the error is\nreported in vendor_rsp[0], and since the function returns 0 the\ntransport will not complete the job a second time.", "datePublished": "2026-09-16T10:31:33", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:53:55", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e25241f9fa01fb0c088381a156d84a725b71c1ef", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0fb52cc632464b0cd07f970341330466d772efe1"], "aliases": ["GHSA-pqg5-73mw-qfjw", "CVE-2026-89862"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.2, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "09c1a84b-b5f9-33d6-8b5b-695954fb3c57", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "871f6236da96c4a9712b8a29d7f555f767a47e95"}, {"id": "1a521f70-a3c4-37c3-b17d-4066d2b5a11e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "1c1f836b-4004-3fb8-bec2-ef4d9de69d3e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.1.164 <6.2"}, {"id": "1d7e9e16-788c-3909-a788-ef74c5e9756b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "708003e1bc857dd014d4c44278d7d77c26f91b1c"}, {"id": "2f045f90-dc26-335e-b9c4-17f3c6618ddd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "c2c68225b1456f4d0d393b5a8778d51bb0d5b1d0 <0fb52cc632464b0cd07f970341330466d772efe1"}, {"id": "31d51aba-0af3-31bf-bfd4-89cb4829d822", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "74e7458537cd9349cf019862e51491f670871707"}, {"id": "32196143-7669-3ad2-a573-1051df843c9d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "c2c68225b1456f4d0d393b5a8778d51bb0d5b1d0 <e25241f9fa01fb0c088381a156d84a725b71c1ef"}, {"id": "3434ac60-ffc3-3fea-a591-dbe2c523b103", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "7.0"}, {"id": "375fb62b-c0a5-34f6-8599-4cd7596bb02d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "31f33b856d2324d86bcaef295f4d210477a1c018"}, {"id": "457b6d86-e48c-30c5-af45-e4a2f6281f14", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "5c1f7c74-0470-3c42-9447-944b156d41f8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.15.201 <5.16"}, {"id": "6e326eb5-030d-34df-8d41-dea7a9355306", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "f2bbb4db0e4a4fbd5e649c0b5d8733f61da24720"}, {"id": "8a42b310-9900-3e0e-be15-059c4a3e659d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.10.251 <5.11"}, {"id": "8c58a613-3f14-3389-8211-442634618b04", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.5"}, {"id": "ac5676b7-11cb-3fc7-b572-6b4c804ddb72", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.12.74 <6.13"}, {"id": "cf57914a-